{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison","id":1325433,"title":"Nova Power Costs Comparison","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-17T17:14:55-07:00","id":1325433,"title":"Nova Power Costs Comparison","content":"So I've seen a few people talk about how super expensive nova powers are. I wanted to bring some perspective to that discussion.<br /> <br /> Thesis: Nova powers have always been super expensive.<br /> <br /> Evidence: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1m94LAcJMq9BsmSgKc3WVqDsYGl6VlgSD8gdSoZrxFnI/edit#gid=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets...FnI/edit#gid=0</a><br /> <br /> If you look at a side-by-side comparison, powers cost significantly more than level 1 powers used to. However, they are only <i>slightly</i> more expensive, on a dot-per-dot basis, than level 2 powers. And there is a significant cost savings on level 3 powers no matter how you slice it. As for Quantum, it's <i>hella</i> cheaper. These things are especially true if you take Nova Points into account.<br /> <br /> 30 Nova Points wasn't very much. At all. With 30 Nova Points, you could get your quantum to 5 and have enough left for... 2 dots in a level 3 power. Or 3 dots in a level 2 power/mega-att and 1 dot in a level 1 power. Or 10 dots of level 1 powers (underwhelming, but I guess claws 5 ain't terrible)<br /> <br /> By contrast, with this system it would cost 64 XP to get to quantum 5. Then you've got 86 XP left over, which is 7 dots of whatever you want... with two XP left, which ain't super useful but hey, Path Edge?<br /> <br /> So. Anyone want me to do math on any of the other traits? Given the multiplicative nature of powers, this cost savings only gets better as time goes by. Especially for powers that get Power tags for free (like Quantum Attack). You wanted an Area Quantum Bolt in 1e at 6 dots, mastered? That's a level 4 power, unless you wait 'til Quantum 6 to buy that Area. Cha-ching.<br /> <br /> Edit: This argument does not stand up if you consider Mega-Edges to be Enhancements, I admit. But Mega-edges are a completely different beast, in a lot of ways... Though yeah, a lot of Mega-Edges cost more than I think they're worth. I'd say they'd be better served by being priced on a separate points scale, and have 12 XP buy you a certain number of points, based on what the Mega-Edges are worth compared to one another. But that's not my call, and I already suggested it in the feedback form.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: I put in the &quot;Dark Star&quot; nova that a lot of people have been super excited about, one with all Mega-Attributes at 1. If you look at a pure XP cost, it's way more expensive now. However if you look at the Nova Point cost, that'd run you 27 NP, leaving you... 3. You can then have... a dot of armor? By contrast, at 108 XP, you've got 42 left over, which gets you 3.5 dots of powers. Or 2 dots of Quantum, and 10 XP remaining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","user":"Jetstream","date":". 07-17-2019, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T18:36:38-07:00","id":1325453,"title":"","content":"The current KS update hints at templates, but a friend of mine has worked out some basic 'templates' people are likely to use.<br /> <br /> &quot;Stealth Nova&quot; Q1, 10 Points in Nova stuff, 30xp remaining<br /> &quot;Nova of All Trades&quot; Q1, 12 points in Nova Stuff, 6xp remaining<br /> &quot;I found the power that I like, so I'm going ALL IN&quot; Q5, 5 dots in one power, 10xp remaining<br /> &quot;Focused Generalist&quot; Q3, 9 dots in Nova Stuff, 10xp remaining<br /> &quot;Less Focused Generalist&quot; Q2, 10 points in Nova Stuff, 14xp remaining<br /> &quot;...I don't quite wanna go all in&quot; Q4, 8 points in Nova Stuff, 6xp remaining<br /> <br /> I also chuckle at the people complaining about the removal of nova points, even as people <i>also</i> complain about how some of the Storyteller games 'still use bonus points instead of XP at chargen'.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T18:46:29-07:00","id":1325457,"title":"","content":"I think the name points of Nova Stuff could be changed to Nova dots. But the options are a good way to see what you can do with 150 XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T19:45:13-07:00","id":1325467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325453#post1325453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current KS update hints at templates, but a friend of mine has worked out some basic 'templates' people are likely to use.<br /> <br /> &quot;Stealth Nova&quot; Q1, 10 Points in Nova stuff, 30xp remaining<br /> &quot;Nova of All Trades&quot; Q1, 12 points in Nova Stuff, 6xp remaining<br /> <b>&quot;I found the power that I like, so I'm going ALL IN&quot; Q5, 5 dots in one power, 10xp remaining</b><br /> &quot;Focused Generalist&quot; Q3, 9 dots in Nova Stuff, 10xp remaining<br /> &quot;Less Focused Generalist&quot; Q2, 10 points in Nova Stuff, 14xp remaining<br /> &quot;...I don't quite wanna go all in&quot; Q4, 8 points in Nova Stuff, 6xp remaining<br /> <br /> I also chuckle at the people complaining about the removal of nova points, even as people <i>also</i> complain about how some of the Storyteller games 'still use bonus points instead of XP at chargen'.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Q5, 5 dots, would actually leave you with 26 XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T19:50:30-07:00","id":1325470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325467#post1325467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Q5, 5 dots, would actually leave you with 26 XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking over things, I think they accidentally had you buying Q1 with that setup, yes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T19:55:04-07:00","id":1325471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325470#post1325470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looking over things, I think they accidentally had you buying Q1 with that setup, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the only way the math would work out like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T20:40:16-07:00","id":1325478,"title":"","content":"So I guess that starting the game with Quantum 1 might be a common thing now in the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T21:28:58-07:00","id":1325484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325478#post1325478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess that starting the game with Quantum 1 might be a common thing now in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why. It's easier to start with higher quantum than it used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T21:33:34-07:00","id":1325486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325484#post1325484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why. It's easier to start with higher quantum than it used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Well then, I guess its just me trying to get as many things as I can and so I found myself being limited in being able to purchase additional Quantum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-18-2019, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T22:59:05-07:00","id":1325500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325478#post1325478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess that starting the game with Quantum 1 might be a common thing now in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too many things are limited by Quantum, if my read is correct you need at least 2 for many of the tags to work. Maxing out also enforces going for high quantum, together with tag stacking rules. Low quantum is the weaker option unless you go for low quantum nova<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T23:41:47-07:00","id":1325505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325500#post1325500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too many things are limited by Quantum, if my read is correct you need at least 2 for many of the tags to work. Maxing out also enforces going for high quantum, together with tag stacking rules. Low quantum is the weaker option unless you go for low quantum nova</div> </div> </div> </div>You're limited by Quantum in terms of how many times you can stack a tag, yes, but you can have as many 1 pointers as you like and that's a lot; a few more are 2 pointers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T23:49:11-07:00","id":1325506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325505#post1325505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're limited by Quantum in terms of how many times you can stack a tag, yes, but you can have as many 1 pointers as you like and that's a lot; a few more are 2 pointers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is what I mean. You need quantum at last 2 for 2 pointers and 3 for three-pointers and so on. Also, a lot of the one pointers you want to stack high. Range, duration, piercing.... Even when provided for free the quantum is still the limit, so You want alway want high quantum on chargen, unless building low quantum nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:31:03-07:00","id":1325564,"title":"","content":"While Quantum 1 is a bit low, more for a Dark Star than a proper Nova, if you rise to quantum 3 you are fine with most of the powers and tags, have a good amount of quantum points and save a good amount of XP for powers and edges. It\u2019s not perfect but it\u2019s balanced.<br /> Higher Quantum is better for one shooter and for focused characters (few powers and more dots), or for characters with highly versatile powers, like Transmutation, Transformation and Quantum Imprint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:59:01-07:00","id":1325576,"title":"","content":"Yeah, getting to Q2-3 is an easy investment. They are great if you are willing to gain the points of Transcendence.<br /> <br /> Though I agree with Jetstream. I am starting to think that mega-edges should cost less, like around 8 XP per dot. Since many of them already require an investment of Mega- Attributes to acquire. <br /> <br /> Another idea I had was that when you purchase a dot of Mega-Attributes you get one free dot to put toward Mega-Edges. This way you can fill in the theme of your character without having to invest so much XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T06:31:03-07:00","id":1325591,"title":"","content":"I did a quick look through to see what kinds of powers a Q1 nova could get, and Morph and Shrink are pretty much the only powers you could put more than one dot into. I do like that you can get to Size -4 with Q1, though. Add in Mega-Might 1, and you have a decent Ant-Man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T07:36:07-07:00","id":1325609,"title":"","content":"You don\u2019t need Mega Might for ant man, he is just as strong as before, but he gets a few enhancements o attacks as he can aim on more critical points.<br /> <br /> Also with hands so small, a punch would be a stab of a very powerful needle... but it would be a bit too bloody for a Disney movie...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T07:43:11-07:00","id":1325610,"title":"","content":"You don't need it, but I believe he technically gets stronger as he shrinks. So, I threw it in there, even though RAW, he could use that full-size as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T08:11:40-07:00","id":1325615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325576#post1325576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, getting to Q2-3 is an easy investment. They are great if you are willing to gain the points of Transcendence.<br /> <br /> Though I agree with Jetstream. I am starting to think that mega-edges should cost less, like around 8 XP per dot. Since many of them already require an investment of Mega- Attributes to acquire. <br /> <br /> Another idea I had was that when you purchase a dot of Mega-Attributes you get one free dot to put toward Mega-Edges. This way you can fill in the theme of your character without having to invest so much XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I don\u2019t think a one-size-fits-all approach works for Mega-edges. That\u2019s why I\u2019m suggesting that XP convert to Mega-Esge Points. That way the edges themselves can have a variable cost while still keeping them unified and under the XP system. 12 XP = X Points. Some things might cost 1 or 2, some might cost the whole amount. Some mega-edges ARE worth 12 XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T08:18:18-07:00","id":1325616,"title":"","content":"Why not have an XP cost assigned to specific Edges. Why add another system of points on top of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T08:20:08-07:00","id":1325617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325616#post1325616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not have an XP cost assigned to specific Edges. Why add another system of points on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because OPP is trying to keep the XP table as simple as possible. Besides, if you're going to go to the trouble of rating the cost of each one, you might as well just balance them all to the same level and give it one XP cost. It would probably be a little more work, but it would keep buying things a lot simpler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T08:20:17-07:00","id":1325618,"title":"","content":"Quick counting here for the Ant-Man.<br /> Q2 (16xp), Shrink 5 (scale -4, 60xp), Growth 2 (scale 3, 24xp), total 100xp, have 50 more to go.<br /> You could go a bit further, add the bestow power as an quantum attack (for the disks), and the Growth momentum, animal mastery for the ants.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s all Q-Tech (or novatech?), so Scott is a Talent using super tech, let\u2019s see what next week manuscript tell about it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T09:51:29-07:00","id":1325631,"title":"","content":"I like how its XP rather then nova points or background points or universe is awesome points or what have you. I think a single experience system is much better than the need to translate one thing to another depending on when or how or why you got something. <br /> <br /> That said I do think some Quantum abilities (especially some Mega-Edges, Body Modification I am looking at you, and maybe even powers and tags) need to have their XP cost looked at.The same with what gets rolled into Mega-Attributes and what needs to be its own system. (Longevity should simply be a Mega-Stamina thing, rather than a power that for most games would not actually be usable.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:33:27-07:00","id":1325679,"title":"","content":"Maybe rather than a completely different set of costs/points for the mega-edges they could be classed into two tiers: 'lesser' and 'greater' (for lack of better terms) and given a different cost for the those two tiers where less powerful/narrower mega-edges could be a bit cheaper while others can be full price. That would provide a little more flexibility in pricing without introducing a whole additional point system or having to determine individual XP costs per Mega-Edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:54:47-07:00","id":1325688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brennanhawkwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325679#post1325679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe rather than a completely different set of costs/points for the mega-edges they could be classed into two tiers: 'lesser' and 'greater' (for lack of better terms) and given a different cost for the those two tiers where less powerful/narrower mega-edges could be a bit cheaper while others can be full price. That would provide a little more flexibility in pricing without introducing a whole additional point system or having to determine individual XP costs per Mega-Edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a \u00bd dot Mega-Edge","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T17:01:00-07:00","id":1325776,"title":"","content":"I think in to solutions to Mega-Edges:<br /> <br /> 1) Except for Mega-Edges not linked to any Attribute/Mega-Attribute (Animal Mastery, Body Modification, Durability, Movement Mode and Q-Tech), all ranked Mega-Edge now have your &quot;level&quot; linked to the Mega-Attribute level.<br /> <i>Example: Inventor now have the same level of Mega-Intelligence, but still costing only 12 XP.</i><br /> <br /> 2) For each dot in a Mega-Attribute you can buy one dot of Mega-Edge having the same Mega-Attribute as pre-requisite for 6 XP.<br /> <i>Example: A Nova have Mega-Intelligence 3, he can buy three dots of Mega-Edge requiring Mega-Intelligence as pre-requisite for 6 XP.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T17:09:16-07:00","id":1325778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadowninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325776#post1325776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in to solutions to Mega-Edges:<br /> <br /> 1) Except for Mega-Edges not linked to any Attribute/Mega-Attribute (Animal Mastery, Body Modification, Durability, Movement Mode and Q-Tech), all ranked Mega-Edge now have your &quot;level&quot; linked to the Mega-Attribute level.<br /> <i>Example: Inventor now have the same level of Mega-Intelligence, but still costing only 12 XP.</i><br /> <br /> 2) For each dot in a Mega-Attribute you can buy one dot of Mega-Edge having the same Mega-Attribute as pre-requisite for 6 XP.<br /> <i>Example: A Nova have Mega-Intelligence 3, he can buy three dots of Mega-Edge requiring Mega-Intelligence as pre-requisite for 6 XP.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really get what you mean by option 1, could you explain further? <br /> <br /> That said I really like Option 2. The idea that your ranks in a Mega-Attribute enhances your ability to get Mega-Edges, thus the cost reduction, is brilliant to me. But what is also cool is that it doesn't stop a person from still being able to buy a Mega-Edge for normal cost. Which means maximum flexibility. <br /> <br /> But yeah the idea that at each Mega-Attribute level you get access to a slightly cheaper Edge sits very well with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T17:20:23-07:00","id":1325784,"title":"","content":"The option 2 is my favored one too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The first option is: You don't need buy levels in Mega-Edges having a Mega-Attribute as pre-requisite. Using the Mega-Edge Inventor as example: <br /> My Nova have Mega-Intelligence 3, I buy Inventor but I don't need buy multiples levels, I use my level in Mega-Intelligence (3 in this example) as the level of Inventor, providing +3 Enhancement to Crafting rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T17:28:18-07:00","id":1325788,"title":"","content":"I like the way it is, it gives more options for character development. You can be super strong with no special tricks. Just a few Mega Edges are weak. <br /> <br /> Also, the way the Mega Edges are, they are not all related to any attribute, so many edges are going to be left from the selection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T18:50:09-07:00","id":1325813,"title":"","content":"Hmm. (That is my thinking noise.)<br /> <br /> Why not have those Mega-Edges that have no prerequisites cost 8XP a pop and those that have pre-requisite cost the full 12. However, each dot you pick up in a mega-Attribute grant you a free dot of a Mege-Edge tied to that Attribute.<br /> <br /> The reason I am for this is that normal edge don't cost all that much in comparison and they certainly don't cost as much as an Attribute dot. You even get a discount based on Path you take. I really think some of the mega-edges are worth the full 12 points. While others should be cheaper, like Body Mod.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also some XP cost needs to be looked at because for 24XP I can grab Mega-Composure 1 and Mental Focus mega-edge. This lets me spent 1 Q point and get my mega-Composure in enhancement to resist outside influences. I could spend 15 XP and no Q points and get +8 Enhancements to resist outside influence. That latter ability is grabbing all three levels of Iron Will and the Indomitable Enhanced Edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2018,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","user":"Bioagent","date":".  added content 07-18-2019, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T12:33:07-07:00","id":1326070,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so. I have been making a few characters and there needs to be a balance/cost change to some of the mega-ages. There is no way that things like Animal Mastery level 1 &amp; 2 (24XP), is worth 2 dots in any actual power or mega-attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T11:28:12-07:00","id":1327474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1325453#post1325453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current KS update hints at templates, but a friend of mine has worked out some basic 'templates' people are likely to use.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Stealth Nova&amp;quot; Q1, 10 Points in Nova stuff, 30xp remaining<br /> &amp;quot;Nova of All Trades&amp;quot; Q1, 12 points in Nova Stuff, 6xp remaining<br /> &amp;quot;I found the power that I like, so I'm going ALL IN&amp;quot; Q5, 5 dots in one power, 10xp remaining<br /> &amp;quot;Focused Generalist&amp;quot; Q3, 9 dots in Nova Stuff, 10xp remaining<br /> &amp;quot;Less Focused Generalist&amp;quot; Q2, 10 points in Nova Stuff, 14xp remaining<br /> &amp;quot;...I don't quite wanna go all in&amp;quot; Q4, 8 points in Nova Stuff, 6xp remaining<br /> <br /> I also chuckle at the people complaining about the removal of nova points, even as people <i>also</i> complain about how some of the Storyteller games 'still use bonus points instead of XP at chargen'.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As the friend in question, I fixed the math and put everything in a google doc here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12sMXOpRiIXSp3Lw9nKtQ51gS7E1POnbAQ2yZjr0jCLE\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...nbAQ2yZjr0jCLE</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T13:22:59-07:00","id":1327480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1325433-nova-power-costs-comparison?p=1326070#post1326070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, so. I have been making a few characters and there needs to be a balance/cost change to some of the mega-ages. There is no way that things like Animal Mastery level 1 &amp; 2 (24XP), is worth 2 dots in any actual power or mega-attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dunno, have you seen what cobra venom can do? Animal Mastery be the kings of the nova world, yo!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12175-sigridhex","name":"SigridHex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}